|PS-02 "SA-02: Remind to take medication"|a1: SA-02 is "Taking prescribed medication"|PS-02 now uses the a1 name

= Open tensions =

No Value Tension has been tested yet, since no Evaluation Method has been run. The table gives each tension's status as recorded on the b2 page, the design stance taken pending evidence, and what is meant to test it.

|=Tension|=Values|=Recorded status|=Stance taken pending evidence|=Tested by
|VT-01 Autonomy vs Well-being|HV-01, HV-05|Provisionally resolved|Graduated support: no assistance while the resident can continue, increasingly supportive prompting when difficulty is detected, and immediate notification of a care worker on an immediate risk of serious harm (group decision, §2.3 Open item O-2). No regulatory floor identified.|UC01-F2-CL4
|VT-02 Privacy vs Well-being|HV-03, HV-05|Provisionally resolved|Monitor only what is needed to decide whether support is needed; share nothing sensitive unless the agreed conditions for caregiver involvement are met. No camera (TECH-04 rejected); Pepper's cameras disabled and covered; the session record is limited to three items and not shared with ST-03.|UC01-F1-CL7, UC01-F4-CL8; record content verified by UC01-F4-PR4 (M-06)
|VT-03 Competence vs Well-being|HV-04, HV-05|Provisionally resolved|Allow time to complete a step, give a supportive prompt on repeated difficulty, and increase assistance if the resident still cannot continue or shows distress.|UC01-F2-CL1, UC01-F2-CL4
|VT-04 Dignity vs Competence|HV-02, HV-04|Open|Prompts phrased as offers in an adult register, addressing the resident by name, stopping as soon as the resident resumes; the robot is framed as a tool with low expressivity. Strained by the choice of Pepper (TECH-01) over the tool-like device (TECH-05), which HFC-05 favours; TECH-05 is the named fallback (§2.3 Open items O-10, O-11).|UC01-F2-CL5 (adverse Claim)
|VT-05 Autonomy vs Well-being (detection reliability)|HV-01, HV-05|Provisionally resolved, open until EM-01 shows an acceptable false-prompt rate|Favour fewer false prompts: F2 waits a configured interval and starts at the least intrusive prompt level. Accepted as the cost of item sensing (TECH-02) without a camera. Timing values are proposals awaiting the first EM-01 pilot (§2.3 Open item O-20).|UC01-F2-PR2 (M-01), UC01-F2-CL4
|VT-06 Autonomy vs Well-being (medication timing)|HV-01, HV-05|Open, deferred to UC02|Deferred with UC02. A floor exists for time-critical medication: residents on such medication are excluded (PS-02), and the source for that floor is still a TODO on the b2 page. DS-02 sketches a resolution for the remaining medication.|No Claim yet; to be written with UC02
|VT-07 Competence vs Attentive care|HV-04, HV-06|Open|The System carries the waiting and the lower prompt levels; the care worker is called only when prompting is exhausted, the resident is distressed, or there is a safety risk (F3). Alert volume is limited by the handover rules grounded on HFC-06 (§2.3 Open item O-22).|UC01-F3-CL9 (M-07), UC01-F3-CL11
|VT-08 Privacy vs Well-being (brushing quality)|HV-03, HV-05|Open|Brushing time is used within the session only and stored nowhere; whether teeth are clean is judged by people (M-08 during evaluation, the home's oral-care routines and ST-05 otherwise). TECH-08 rejected; TECH-07 deferred until EM-02 shows whether brushing time is enough. Part of §2.3 Open item O-23 is still open (per-resident targets, confirming the plaque instrument).|UC01-F1-CL7, UC01-F3-CL11; TECH-07 decision also depends on UC01-F2-CL10

= Completeness check =

== Checks the manual names ==

|=Check|=Result|=Stance
|Any Situated Activity with no Goal stated|None. SA-01, SA-02 and SA-03 each state a Goal.|SA-02's Goal is addressed only by TECH-06, which is deferred with UC02 (§2.3 Open item O-13). Recorded as a scope decision for this cycle.
|Any Human Value with no recognition criteria|None. HV-01 to HV-06 each state served and violated criteria.|No action.
|Any Human Factors Concept with no associated Measure|None. HFC-01 to HFC-06 each name at least one Measure.|No action. The reverse links on the Measures page have been completed (see //One-sided and inconsistent edges//).
|Any Technology Option addressing nothing|The three selected options (TECH-01 to TECH-03) each address a Goal or Human Value. The five rejected or deferred options (TECH-04 to TECH-08) have no "addresses" edge, which follows from their status. In their Benefits fields, TECH-04 names Goal (SA-01), TECH-06 names Goal (SA-02) and TECH-07 names HV-05; TECH-05 now names HV-02 and HV-03, and TECH-08 names HV-05.|Fixed on the c1 page, so that every option, rejected or not, states what it would have served.

== Further gaps ==

|=Gap|=Stance
|SA-02, PS-02, VT-06 and TECH-06 form one cluster with no Claim, no Measure and no Evaluation Method.|Deferred with UC02 (§2.3 Open item O-13). New Measures for it start at M-09 and new Evaluation Methods at EM-04 (§2.3 Open item O-1).
|VT-06 has no testing Claim.|Deferred with UC02, as above. Every other tension has at least one testing Claim or Premise.
|HV-01 Autonomy and HV-02 Dignity are not addressed by any selected Technology Option.|Both are carried by Function behaviour: F2's wait and offer-style prompts follow the VT-01, VT-03 and VT-04 resolutions. They are tested by UC01-F2-CL3 (HV-01) and UC01-F2-CL5 (HV-02).
|No Technology Option addresses the Goal on SA-03 directly.|SA-03's Goal reaches the design through HV-06 (addressed by TECH-01 and TECH-03) and OBJ-06. Recorded.
|ST-03, ST-04 and ST-05 have no Persona and perform no Situated Activity.|All three are Indirect Stakeholders. A Persona is built for Direct Stakeholders only, and both Direct Stakeholders have one (ST-01 → HP-01, ST-02 → HP-02). No action.
|M-08 Brushing quality has no associated Human Factors Concept.|M-08 is justified through VT-08 and HV-05, and was added for the midterm feedback (§2.3 Open item O-23). Recorded; no HFC is proposed for this cycle.
|Every Foundation entity is provisional: no resident, care worker or manager has been observed or interviewed.|Recorded on every Evidence basis field (§2.3 Open item O-17). The edges on this page inherit that status.
|Premise thresholds and escalation timing are proposals.|Pending the first EM-01 pilot (§2.3 Open item O-20). Affects VT-05's stance.
|Whether Pepper (TECH-01) fits at a care-home bathroom doorway is unchecked.|§2.3 Open item O-21; fallback is TECH-05. Affects TECH-01's feasibility and the VT-04 stance.

= Status of these edges =

These edges are a hypothesis about fit between the operational demands, the human values and human factors, and the technology. They are to be confirmed or revised once the System and its Use Cases are evaluated: the forward edges into UC01 name the Premises and Claims that will do so, and the UC02 cluster stays unconnected until UC02 is specified.
